{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Observations.TraceRatioObservable","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Observations.TraceRatioObservable","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Intervals","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.trace_ratio_observable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.trace_ratio_observable","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/trace-ratio-observable.lean#L52-L82","doc":"The trace ratio observable: the beta-decay matrix element squared\nis proportional to the product of volume ratios over affected\ngenerators, times the Skein amplitude squared.\n\n|M_q|² ∝ |skein_amp|² · ∏_{i=0}^{p} |V̂_i^par / V̂_i^dau|².\n\nThis is the main proposition: the exponential growth of individual\nMarkov traces cancels in the ratio, leaving a finite product over\nonly the generators affected by the nucleon conversion. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:trace-ratio-observable","label":"prop:trace-ratio-observable","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/trace-ratio-observable.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.generator_cancellation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.generator_cancellation","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/trace-ratio-observable.lean#L44-L50","doc":"Generators i > p cancel between parent and daughter:\nif V_par i = V_dau i then the ratio is 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.trace_ratio_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.trace_ratio_product","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/trace-ratio-observable.lean#L38-L42","doc":"The trace ratio product over affected generators 0..p:\n∏_{i=0}^{p} |V̂_i^par / V̂_i^dau|². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skein_amp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skein_amp","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/trace-ratio-observable.lean#L33-L36","doc":"The Skein amplitude for a single beta decay vertex:\ns = q^{1/2} - q^{-1/2}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.traced_generator_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.traced_generator_volume","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/trace-ratio-observable.lean#L27-L31","doc":"The Markov-traced generator volume at generator σ_i:\nV̂_i = z · a_i + b_i, where z is the Markov parameter and\na_i, b_i are the crossing-dependent coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0}]}